// Two bollards side by side: a prefab with prefabs inside it.
//
// Each bollard here is an instance of prefabs/bollard.prefab.json, placed in this prefab as
// it would be placed in a scene: its root has a PrefabInstance, and every entity of it a
// PrefabLink to the entity of the bollard prefab it is a copy of. Those links stay in this
// file. Whatever reads it - the editor placing it, or bringing what was placed of it up to
// date, a script placing it - first brings the bollards in here up to date with the bollard
// prefab, but for what this file keeps of its own: so a change to a bollard reaches every
// pair, and this file need not be written again for it.
//
// What this file keeps of its own is said, as in a scene: the right bollard has no cap,
// which its cap's link lists as "enabled". A prefab that held itself, directly or through
// others, would be refused, the chain of files named.
